-- Sync locations.latitude/longitude/radius_meters against the Azambuja
-- TRACKiT account's POI reference (data/azambuja_poi_reference.csv),
-- confirmed by the user to be keyed by the official Auchan store code.
--
-- Background: that CSV's `code` is a "bare" number/string (12, 14, 24, 25...)
-- that can collide with unrelated codes in our `locations` table that have
-- nothing to do with the Auchan network. A matching code alone was NOT
-- treated as sufficient evidence — see scripts/compare-azambuja-poi.ts,
-- which for every code-match also compares `locations.name` against the
-- POI name (accent/case-insensitive, "auchan"/"my"/"ma"/"pb" treated as
-- brand-prefix noise) and only counts it a real match above a 0.5
-- token-overlap similarity. That produced two groups:
--
--   - data/azambuja-poi-safe-matches.csv (165 rows): name matches, only
--     coordinate/radius differ -> real candidates to update.
--   - data/azambuja-poi-name-collisions.csv (14 rows): code matches but the
--     name has nothing to do with it -> different systems colliding on a
--     bare numeric code. NOT touched by this or any migration; left for the
--     user to resolve case by case.
--
-- Of the 165 safe matches, 11 have our coordinate and the POI coordinate
-- more than 5km apart even though the name matches exactly (e.g. I104
-- "Caves Avelar" vs itself, 34km apart). Large distance + exact name match
-- is still consistent with "our coordinate is simply wrong", but the user
-- asked to hold these back for manual confirmation on a map before
-- applying, rather than trust the diff blindly:
--
--   I104, 243A, M065, I958, 729, B100, I402, 63, I691, I534, 368
--
-- This migration applies only the remaining 154 rows (distance <= 5km).
--
-- Radius: 4 of the 154 rows have a POI radius of 0m (403, 7001, 18, 718).
-- 0m would effectively disable proximity matching for that location, which
-- reads as "no radius configured" in the source rather than a real value —
-- so for those four, radius_meters is left unchanged; only lat/lng update.
--
-- PREVIEW — run first to sanity check row count before applying:
--
--   select count(*) from locations where code in (
--     '711','703','B12','283','N126','327','708','244','461','C763','724',
